        "original_id": "3c9b9a63-2481-5510-8b50-2b9a614c91b9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lake Wobegon Trails, central Minnesota, Saint Paul, New York City\n- Works: Lake Wobegon, A Prairie Home Companion\n- People: Garrison Keillor\n- Topics: recreational rail trails, radio broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- The Lake Wobegon Trails are two paved recreational rail trails in central Minnesota.\n- The Lake Wobegon Trails are named after the fictional Lake Wobegon in Garrison Keillor's A Prairie Home Companion.\n- A Prairie Home Companion airs on Saturdays from 5 to 7 p.m. Central Time from the Fitzgerald Theater in Saint Paul, Minnesota.\n- A Prairie Home Companion is also frequently heard on tours to New York City and other United States cities.",
